  "theory_modules": 41,
  "scope": "Complete area and weighted area formulas for Lipschitz maps in the printed m<=n setting, with supporting theorems valid for all ambient dimensions. Arbitrary measurable source sets, infinite integral values and original partial integrand domains are retained. Actual Jacobian measurability, Borel partition multiplicity sums, the injective rank case and geometric squeeze, graph-lift singular Jacobian and critical-image-null proof, finite and countable Borel reductions, characteristic-series weighted formula, bounded-Jacobian preservation of a finite variation, and exact abstract/proved/opaque partial numerical fibre sums are proved. Three regressions cover empty fibres, undefined nonempty fibres and the positive-infinite weighted integrand. Apply erratum p. 4, book p. 244 line 11: J_m f(x).",
  "source_count_checked_unchanged": 6249,
